1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,250
The anti consumerist stands of tyler durden becomes obvious when he verbalizes his concern about a modern way of life.
作者说，泰勒·德顿表达对现代生活方式的看法时，他的反消费主义立场就显现出来。

2
00:00:08,250 --> 00:00:14,050
Shortly after the narrator meets tyler he discovers that his apartment went up in flames.
故事中，叙述者遇见泰勒不久后，就发现自己的公寓毁于大火。

3
00:00:14,050 --> 00:00:19,980
After this unfortunate event realizing that he has no friends to call he calls tyler.
经历这件不幸的事后，他发现没有朋友可联系，于是给泰勒打电话。

4
00:00:19,990 --> 00:00:28,050
The two meet and a narrator complains about losing his furniture and his respectable and almost complete wardrobe.
两人见面，叙述者抱怨失去了家具和那套体面、几乎齐全的衣橱。

5
00:00:28,060 --> 00:00:35,230
Tyler responds rather in differently and slightly sarcastically before he begins to express his views on the matter.
泰勒态度冷淡，又略带讽刺，随后开始表达自己的看法。

6
00:00:35,230 --> 00:00:40,600
I quote where consumers we are byproducts of a lifestyle obsession.
作者接着引用角色的话：我们是消费者，是痴迷某种生活方式的副产品。

7
00:00:40,600 --> 00:00:44,550
Murder crime poverty these things don't concern me.
角色说，谋杀、犯罪、贫穷这些事不让他在意。

8
00:00:44,560 --> 00:00:55,150
What concerns me are celebrity magazines television with 500 channels some guy's name on my underwear rogaine viagra olestra and quote.
他反而在意名人杂志、500个电视频道、衣物品牌以及各种消费品；引文结束。

9
00:00:55,150 --> 00:01:00,579
It becomes clear that tyler has quite an unconventional view of what's good and bad.
作者认为，泰勒对好坏有一种很不寻常的理解。

10
00:01:00,579 --> 00:01:05,230
Murder crime and poverty are generally considered bad things.
谋杀、犯罪和贫穷通常被视为坏事。

11
00:01:05,230 --> 00:01:09,220
While consumer goods like televisions clothing from a certain brand.
而电视、某个品牌的服装等消费品……

12
00:01:09,220 --> 00:01:16,530
Products that help to hide aging enhance bedroom performance and help us with weight loss are considered preferable.
以及掩饰衰老、改善性表现、帮助减重的产品，通常被认为是较好的东西。

13
00:01:16,530 --> 00:01:24,530
Tyler has a contempt for the artificial as opposed to elements have been a natural part of the human condition probably as long as we exist.
作者说，泰勒蔑视人工制造的东西，反而看重伴随人类长久存在的自然部分。

14
00:01:24,540 --> 00:01:30,579
This way of thinking touches upon an ancient cynic philosopher named diogenes of sinope ii.
作者把这种想法与古代犬儒派哲学家第欧根尼联系起来。

15
00:01:30,579 --> 00:01:34,800
Who believed that modern civilized life hinders our natural state.
他介绍说，第欧根尼认为现代文明生活妨碍人的自然状态。

16
00:01:34,810 --> 00:01:40,060
At the end of the movie it appears that a narrator has destroyed his apartment himself.
影片结尾似乎表明，公寓实际上是叙述者自己毁掉的。

17
00:01:40,060 --> 00:01:43,690
When he was taken over by his alter ego tyler durden.
当时他被另一个自我——泰勒·德顿——控制。

18
00:01:43,690 --> 00:01:50,560
This deed was the first step onto the road of detachment from his property into a more authentic way of life.
作者把这一行为解读为摆脱财物、走向更真实生活的第一步。

19
00:01:50,560 --> 00:01:58,349
And to how tyler puts it reject the basic assumptions of civilization especially the importance of material possessions.
用泰勒的话说，就是拒绝文明的基本假设，尤其是对物质财产的看重。

20
00:01:58,359 --> 00:02:06,840
The narrator moves in with tyler who lives in a dilapidated house with ongoing leaks power failures and no ikea furniture.
叙述者搬去与泰勒同住，房屋破败、漏水、断电，也没有宜家家具。

21
00:02:06,840 --> 00:02:13,230
Slowly but surely the narrator indeed detaches from his previously destroyed property.
慢慢地，叙述者确实不再依恋那些已被毁掉的财物。

22
00:02:13,230 --> 00:02:17,410
Things you own end up owning you tyler tells him.
泰勒告诉他：你拥有的东西，最终反而会拥有你。

23
00:02:17,410 --> 00:02:30,270
And the simple piece of wisdom probably hits home when the narrator realizes that he doesn't need all these worldly goods and is actually much happier without them.
当他意识到不需要那些世俗物品、没有它们反而更开心时，这句话似乎真正触动了他。

24
00:02:30,280 --> 00:02:36,180
Tyler durden is a nonconformist and shows again similarities with diogenes.
作者说，泰勒是个不顺从常规的人，这又与第欧根尼有相似之处。

25
00:02:36,190 --> 00:02:40,560
Who not only purposefully lived in poverty but also rejected social norms.
第欧根尼不仅有意过贫穷生活，也拒绝社会规范。

26
00:02:40,570 --> 00:02:48,599
For him social constructs are nothing more than a superficial layer of culture that represses our true nature.
按作者的介绍，这种观点把社会建构视为压抑真实天性的表层文化。

27
00:02:48,609 --> 00:02:53,099
Diogenes lived in a barrel tyler lives in an abandoned building.
作者对照说，第欧根尼住在桶里，泰勒住在废弃建筑中。

28
00:02:53,109 --> 00:02:58,050
Diogenes urinated in public tyler urinates in the soup of a restaurant.
他继续对比两者的冒犯行为：一个在公共场所小便，另一个在餐厅汤里小便。

29
00:02:58,060 --> 00:03:03,639
Diogenes bit his opponents like a dog tyler salivates over them using his own blood.
作者还对照咬人、用血挑衅对手等行为，说明角色的极端性。

30
00:03:03,639 --> 00:03:11,950
The narrator on the other hand seems to be the embodiment of conformity as he adapts his lifestyle completely to societal expectations.
另一边，叙述者似乎是从众的化身，把生活完全调整成符合社会期待的样子。

31
00:03:11,950 --> 00:03:19,930
The problem with this behavior is that we dedicate our existence walking the paths that people other than ourselves have laid out for us.
作者认为，这样的问题在于，人把一生用来走别人替自己规划的路。

32
00:03:19,930 --> 00:03:27,870
This need to conform this fear of falling by the wayside this sickly preoccupation by what others think of us.
想从众、害怕被落下、过度在意别人的看法……

33
00:03:27,880 --> 00:03:34,889
This necessity to keep up with the joneses what an exhausting way of life just to feel accepted.
为了攀比、为了被接纳，作者感叹这是多么累的一种生活。

34
00:03:34,889 --> 00:03:42,480
So what if we stop caring what if we reject the generally accepted norms and choose our own values.
那么，如果不再在意、拒绝公认的规范，选择自己的价值观呢？

35
00:03:42,490 --> 00:03:48,759
Elect our own leaders determine our own goals regardless of the social expectations.
自己选领导者、定目标，不受社会期待左右，会怎样？

36
00:03:48,759 --> 00:03:54,220
This is a fundamental difference between the narrator and tyler durden who puts it like this.
作者说，这是叙述者与泰勒之间的根本差别，泰勒这样形容：

37
00:03:54,220 --> 00:03:57,710
I am free in all the ways that you are not.
角色说：在你不自由的所有方面，我都是自由的。

38
00:03:57,720 --> 00:04:04,960
Ironically later on in the story project man a terrorist organization led by tyler that grows out of fight club.
但讽刺的是，故事后来从搏击俱乐部发展出的泰勒所领导的恐怖组织……

39
00:04:04,960 --> 00:04:07,749
Is a textbook example of conformity.
却成了一个典型的从众案例。

40
00:04:07,749 --> 00:04:14,619
As its members wear the same clothes are absolutely equal abolish their names and are referred to as space monkeys.
成员穿相同服装、完全平等、取消姓名，被称作太空猴。

41
00:04:14,619 --> 00:04:17,470
That sacrifice their lives for a greater cause.
他们为一个所谓更大的事业牺牲生命。

42
00:04:17,470 --> 00:04:26,260
We could say that by rejecting one doctrine in order to be nonconformist we often imprison ourselves in another one.
作者总结：为摆脱从众而拒绝一种教条时，我们往往又把自己囚禁在另一种教条里。
